---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use | LocalPDF';
const description = 'Read the LocalPDF Terms of Use for subscriptions, license keys, acceptable use, disclaimers, and service limitations.';
const canonical = 'https://localpdf.online/terms';
const image = 'https://localpdf.online/logos/localpdf-social-1200x630.png';
const termsSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: title,
  description,
  url: canonical,
};
---

<MarketingLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} image={image} schema={termsSchema}>
  <div class="page-shell legal-shell">
    <section class="section intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Terms</span>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="section-intro">
        These Terms of Use govern your access to the LocalPDF website, app, and paid plans. By using LocalPDF or purchasing a subscription,
        you agree to these terms.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: 2026-03-22</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">1. Who operates LocalPDF</h2>
      <p>
        LocalPDF is operated through the website at <a href="https://localpdf.online">localpdf.online</a>. For support, billing questions,
        privacy requests, or legal notices, contact <a href="mailto:support@localpdf.online">support@localpdf.online</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">2. What LocalPDF provides</h2>
      <p>
        LocalPDF provides PDF tools and document workflows, including editing, merging, OCR, conversion, protection, and related functionality.
        Some features may be available for free, and some require a paid Pro subscription or a valid license state.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may update, improve, suspend, replace, or remove features over time. We may also change packaging, usage limits, pricing, and plan
        structure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">3. Accounts, subscriptions, and license keys</h2>
      <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li>Paid access may be sold as a monthly or yearly Pro subscription.</li>
        <li>Checkout and billing may be handled by our payment provider, LemonSqueezy.</li>
        <li>After purchase, you may receive a license key or equivalent subscription credential.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for keeping your license key secure.</li>
        <li>License keys are personal to the purchaser or intended customer and may not be resold, sublicensed, or shared abusively.</li>
        <li>We may limit, suspend, or revoke access in cases of fraud, abuse, payment reversal, or misuse of the licensing system.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">4. Renewals and cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        If a Pro plan is sold as a recurring subscription, it renews automatically until canceled through the payment provider or applicable customer portal.
        Canceling stops future renewals but does not retroactively reverse charges already processed, unless required by law or covered by our refund policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Additional billing and refund details are described on the <a href="/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li>You may use LocalPDF only for lawful purposes.</li>
        <li>You must not process documents you do not have the right to handle.</li>
        <li>You must not attempt to bypass feature restrictions, licensing checks, or technical safeguards.</li>
        <li>You must not reverse engineer, abuse, disrupt, overload, or interfere with the service.</li>
        <li>You must not use LocalPDF to infringe intellectual property, privacy, or confidentiality rights.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">6. Document accuracy and user responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        PDF editing, OCR, conversion, extraction, compression, and redaction-related workflows can produce imperfect results. You are responsible for reviewing
        output files before relying on them for business, legal, financial, compliance, or archival purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        You should keep your own backups of important files. LocalPDF is a productivity tool, not a substitute for your own validation, document controls,
        or records policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">7. Privacy and data handling</h2>
      <p>
        Our handling of personal data is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. By using LocalPDF, you acknowledge that payment,
        analytics, support, and technical operations may involve third-party services described there.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        LocalPDF, its branding, site content, software, and related materials are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. Except where allowed by law,
        you may not copy, distribute, modify, sell, or exploit our software or site content without permission.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        LocalPDF is provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis. To the maximum extent permitted by law, we disclaim warranties of merchantability,
        fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, uninterrupted availability, and error-free operation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">10. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, LocalPDF will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for loss of
        profits, revenue, data, business, goodwill, or documents arising from or related to your use of the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, our total liability for claims related to paid services will not exceed the amount you paid for LocalPDF in the
        12 months before the event giving rise to the claim.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">11. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The updated version becomes effective when posted on this page unless stated otherwise.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section final-band">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Related pages</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Need the practical policy pages too?</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Read Privacy for data handling, Refund Policy for billing questions, and Security for a plain-language explanation of local-first document handling.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/privacy">Read Privacy</a>
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="/refund-policy">Read Refund Policy</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 940px;
  }

  .intro h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 5vw, 4.8rem);
    margin-top: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .meta {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .legal-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .final-band {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
  }
</style>
